  "notes": "Governmental funds on a modified cash basis (Total Governmental Funds 2023 column printed on p6, labels on p5; balance sheet totals on p4); proprietary funds on the accrual basis (measure net position; the proprietary cash flow statement p9 is not recorded in 'proprietary' because the report basis is cash). Fund balances recorded as fund balance; cash = cash in bank + cash with county treasurer, certificates of deposit as investments (p4, 2023 and 2022 columns). Statement lines split with the report's own fund schedules: Taxes 33,793 = General property 2,714 + motor vehicle 3,549 (p10) + Street property 17,321 + county road tax 1,478 (p14) + nonmajor property 8,731 (p12) (Statement of Activities also prints Taxes 30,244 + Motor vehicle tax 3,549); Intergovernmental revenues 111,501 = General 42,379 (p10) + Street 69,122 (p14); Charges for services 43,895 = Schedule 2 licenses 4,214 + materials and services sold 38,454 + sales tax collected 1,227. No transfers. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1), because its governmental column includes capital assets 894,238 not in the governmental funds statement. Detail: Schedule 2 (General Fund), Schedule 4 (Fire, Cemetery), Schedule 6 (Street, Keno Lottery), Schedule 8 (proprietary funds combined, Actual column). Not recorded to avoid double counting: Schedule 7 budget comparison (fund totals only, budget-basis Keno gross receipts) and Schedule 9 Keno budget-basis reconciliation; Schedules 3 and 5 are balance sheets. Read pages 1-17 of 17"
}
